; pdf -- writing PDF files: a document of pages carrying text, rules, filled
; rectangles and images, with named destinations and page labels. Text is
; UTF-8, in the standard fonts every reader has or in TrueType fonts the
; document embeds with the glyphs it uses. No library is needed: an image
; goes in as its file holds it, and the one that cannot -- a PNG with an
; alpha channel -- is decoded here. What is written is PDF 1.4.
;
; The modules, in dependency order: the width table of the standard fonts
; (generated), the standard fonts, the decoder, the TrueType reader, the
; index of font files, the document.

package scaly 0.1.0

define pdf
{
    module Metrics
    module Font
    module Inflate
    module TrueType
    module FontFiles
    module Document
}
